# known_hosts for this device — kept in the repo on purpose.
#
# The device's sshd host key is PINNED to keys/gemini_ed25519 (see the SSH
# section of config/gemini.nix), not generated per install, so this entry
# stays valid across a from-scratch reflash: no "REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION
# HAS CHANGED" after reinstalling. Use it with:
#
#   ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=keys/known_hosts root@10.15.19.82
#
# (bin/device-ssh.sh and friends deliberately run with
# StrictHostKeyChecking=no + UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null — a flash must
# never be blocked by host-key state — so they neither need nor touch this
# file. It exists so a human/tool CAN verify against the repo.)
#
# Keep it in sync with the key (bin/flash-nixos.sh preflight checks this):
#   ssh-keygen -y -f keys/gemini_ed25519
10.15.19.82 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIAfbrOwr8K31h6e+4kE/cdz++DQlDHkF7Vd/n4Y0/KhH
